</math> inches less than <math alttext="7"><mn>7</mn>
</math> times its width, or <math alttext="7 x minus 4"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mn>7</mn>
		<mi>x</mi>
	</mrow>
	<mo>-</mo>
	<mn>4</mn>
</mrow>
</math> inches. The area of a rectangle is equal to its width multiplied by its length. Multiplying the width, <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> inches, by the length, <math alttext="7 x minus 4"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mn>7</mn>
		<mi>x</mi>
	</mrow>
	<mo>-</mo>
	<mn>4</mn>
</mrow>
</math> inches, yields <math alttext="x left parenthesis 7 x minus 4 right parenthesis"><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> square inches. It&rsquo;s given that the rectangle has an area of <math alttext="155"><mn>155</mn>
</math> square inches, so it follows that <math alttext="x left parenthesis 7 x minus 4 right parenthesis equals 155"><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>155</mn></math>, or <math alttext="7 x squared minus 4 x equals 155"><mn>7</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>155</mn></math>. Subtracting <math alttext="155"><mn>155</mn>
</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext="7 x squared minus 4 x minus 155 equals 0"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mn>7</mn>
			<msup>
				<mi>x</mi>
				<mn>2</mn>
			</msup>
		</mrow>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mrow>
			<mn>4</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mn>155</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Factoring the left-hand side of this equation yields&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis 7 x plus 31 right parenthesis left parenthesis x minus 5 right parenthesis equals 0"><mfenced><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>31</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Applying the zero product property to this equation yields two solutions: <math alttext="x equals negative StartFraction 31 Over 7 EndFraction"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>31</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math> and <math alttext="x equals 5"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>5</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Since <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> is the rectangle&rsquo;s width, in inches, which must be positive, the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math>. Therefore, the width of the rectangle, in inches, is <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"7a6d06bf","external_id":"6e108e29-0eee-4507-8a4a-45c4b2c82383","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"d3b99e45-ec98-494a-8b38-f70a75683300","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A rectangle has an area of <math alttext=\"155\"><mn>155</mn>\n</math> square inches. The length of the rectangle is <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> inches less than <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> times the width of the rectangle. What is the width of the rectangle, in inches?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["5"],"correct_answer":["5"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math>. Let <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> represent the width, in inches, of the rectangle. It's given that the length of the rectangle is <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> inches less than <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> times its width, or <math alttext=\"7 x minus 4\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches. The area of a rectangle is equal to its width multiplied by its length. Multiplying the width, <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> inches, by the length, <math alttext=\"7 x minus 4\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches, yields <math alttext=\"x left parenthesis 7 x minus 4 right parenthesis\"><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> square inches. It&rsquo;s given that the rectangle has an area of <math alttext=\"155\"><mn>155</mn>\n</math> square inches, so it follows tha