    ($SATQ$7ba694f3$SATQ$, $SATQ$d1baa89a-a42c-46e1-a485-7574f59a8753$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$2423923f-925f-494c-be15-fe4b27e0d515$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p>The number of bacteria in a liquid medium doubles every day. There are <math alttext="44,000"><mn>44,000</mn>
</math> bacteria in the liquid medium at the start of an observation. Which represents the number of bacteria, <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math>, in the liquid medium <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math><em>&nbsp;</em>days after the start of the observation?&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"05fe3d13-1119-41cf-9145-09f74be4ae24","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals one half left parenthesis 44,000 right parenthesis Superscript t\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>44,000</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>t</mi></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"f8f4d50a-4222-4afc-94e5-c06734184203","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals 2 left parenthesis 44,000 right parenthesis Superscript t\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>44,000</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>t</mi></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"bb20698d-b1c7-42bf-bfaf-5e34a64059ec","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals 44,000 left parenthesis one half right parenthesis Superscript t\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>44,000</mn></mrow><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>t</mi></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"6c27247d-60c2-4c14-95c6-d477c47cccb4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals 44,000 left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis Superscript t\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>44,000</mn></mrow><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mi>t</mi></msup></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["6c27247d-60c2-4c14-95c6-d477c47cccb4"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. Since the number of bacteria doubles every day, the relationship between <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> can be represented by an exponential equation of the form <math alttext="y equals a left parenthesis b right parenthesis Superscript t"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mi>b</mi></mfenced><mi>t</mi></msup></math>, where <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math> is the number of bacteria at the start of the observation and the number of bacteria increases by a factor of <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> every day. It&rsquo;s given that there are <math alttext="44,000"><mn>44,000</mn>
</math> bacteria at the start of the observation. Therefore, <math alttext="a equals 44,000"><mrow>
	<mi>a</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>44,000</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. It&rsquo;s also given that the number of bacteria doubles, or increases by a factor of <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math>, every day. Therefore, <math alttext="b equals 2"><mrow>
	<mi>b</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>2</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="44,000"><mn>44,000</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> in the equation <math alttext="y equals a left parenthesis b right parenthesis Superscript t"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mi>b</mi></mfenced><mi>t</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;yields <math alttext="y equals 44,000 left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis Superscript t"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>44,000</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mi>t</mi></msup></math>.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect. This equation represents a situation where the number of bacteria is decreasing by half, not doubling, every day.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"7ba694f3","external_id":"d1baa89a-a42c-46e1-a485-7574f59a8753","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"2423923f-925f-494c-be15-fe4b27e0d515","uId":"a1f76398-0aec-4592-821b-537775e3d775","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p>The number of bacteria in a liquid medium doubles every day. There are <math alttext=\"44,000\"><mn>44,000</mn>\n</math> bacteria in the liquid medium at the start of an observation. Which represents the number of bacteria, <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>, in the liquid medium <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math><em>&nbsp;</em>days after the start of the observation?&nbsp;</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"05fe3d13-1119-41cf-9145-09f74be4ae24","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals one half left parenthesis 44,000 right parenthesis Superscript t\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>44,000</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>t</mi></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"f8f4d50a-4222-4afc-94e5-c06734184203","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals 2 left parenthesis 44,000 right parenthesis Superscript t\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>44,000</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>t</mi></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"bb20698d-b1c7-42bf-bfaf-5e34a64059ec","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals 44,000 left parenthesis one half right parenthesis Superscript t\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>44,000</mn></mrow><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>t</mi></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"6c27247d-60c2-4c14-95c6-d477c47cccb4","content":"<p><math alttext