i>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> has <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> unique solutions: <math alttext=\"x equals d\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mi>d</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"x equals negative d\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mi>d</mi>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"x equals negative g\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mi>g</mi>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Thus, the graph of the given equation has <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> distinct <em>x</em>-intercepts.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1743430554980,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"7e6ea718","skill_cd":"P.C.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","createDate":1743430554980,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"","external_id":"230aed17-3fcc-4941-9290-a69a66f31d95","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"f0ffbbf5-5e13-42da-8aa5-a91a9992b049","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 2 left parenthesis x minus d right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus d right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus g right parenthesis left parenthesis x minus d right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>d</mi>\n<mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi>\n<mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi>\n<mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>d</mi>\n<mo>)</mo></math></p>\n