$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p>1</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p>0</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_000_ebe7b417.png\" alt=\"negative 2\"></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_001_22df6a62.png\" alt=\"negative 5\"></span></p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is correct. Applying the distributive property on the left- and right-hand sides of the given equation yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_003_5ff504dd.png" alt="x squared, plus 2 x, plus 3 x, plus 6, equals, x squared, minus 2 x, minus 3 x, plus 6, plus 10"></span>, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_004_96ea0052.png" alt="x squared, plus 5 x, plus 6, equals, x squared, minus 5 x, plus 16"></span>. Subtracting <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_005_572bc813.png" alt="x squared "></span> from and adding <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_006_ec342366.png" alt="5 x"></span> to both sides of this equation yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_007_569961e7.png" alt="10 x plus 6, equals 16"></span>. Subtracting 6 from both sides of this equation and then dividing both sides by 10 yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_008_70a1cc99.png" alt="x equals 1"></span>.<p>Choices B, C, and D are incorrect. Substituting 0, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_009_ebe7b417.png" alt="negative 2"></span>, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_010_22df6a62.png" alt="negative 5"></span> for <span class="italic">x</span> in the given equation will result in a false statement. If <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_011_3f34714f.png" alt="x equals 0"></span>, the given equation becomes <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_012_7d2ee910.png" alt="6 equals 16"></span>; if <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_013_3fa4dcee.png" alt="x equals negative 2"></span>, the given equation becomes <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_014_a1f00a8b.png" alt="0 equals 30"></span>; and if <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_015_16898e9a.png" alt="x equals negative 5"></span>, the given equation becomes <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_016_0d82e2b9.png" alt="6 equals 66"></span>. Therefore, the values 0, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_017_ebe7b417.png" alt="negative 2"></span>, and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_018_22df6a62.png" alt="negative 5"></span> aren&rsquo;t solutions to the given equation.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 19, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"802549ac","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"027749-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.B.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_002_9223e4f5.png\" alt=\"open parenthesis, x plus 2, close parenthesis, times, open parenthesis, x plus 3, close parenthesis, equals, open parenthesis, x minus 2, close parenthesis, times, open parenthesis, x minus 3, close parenthesis, plus 10\"></span></span></p></div>\n","stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Which of the following is a solution to the given equation?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p>1</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p>0</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_000_ebe7b417.png\" alt=\"negative 2\"></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_001_22df6a62.png\" alt=\"negative 5\"></span></p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. Applying the distributive property on the left- and right-hand sides of the given equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_003_5ff504dd.png\" alt=\"x squared, plus 2 x, plus 3 x, plus 6, equals, x squared, minus 2 x, minus 3 x, plus 6, plus 10\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_004_96ea0052.png\" alt=\"x squared, plus 5 x, plus 6, equals, x squared, minus 5 x, plus 16\"></span>. Subtracting <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_005_572bc813.png\" alt=\"x squared \"></span> from and adding <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_006_ec342366.png\" alt=\"5 x\"></span> to both sides of this equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_007_569961e7.png\" alt=\"10 x plus 6, equals 16\"></span>. Subtracting 6 from both sides of this equation and then dividing both sides by 10 yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_008_70a1cc99.png\" alt=\"x equals 1\"></span>.<p>Choices B, C, and D are incorrect. Substituting 0, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_009_ebe7b417.png\" alt=\"negative 2\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_010_22df6a62.png\" alt=\"negative 5\"></span> for <span class=\"italic\">x</span> in the given equation will result in a false statement. If <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_011_3f34714f.png\" alt=\"x equals 0\"></span>, the given equation becomes <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_012_7d2ee910.png\" alt=\"6 equals 16\"></span>; if <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_013_3fa4dcee.png\" alt=\"x equals negative 2\"></span>, the given equation becomes <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_014_a1f00a8b.png\" alt=\"0 equals 30\"></span>; and if <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_015_16898e9a.png\" alt=\"x equals negative 5\"></span>, the given equation becomes <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_016_0d82e2b9.png\" alt=\"6 equals 66\"></span>. Therefore, the values 0, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_017_ebe7b417.png\" alt=\"negative 2\"></span>, and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/802549ac/img_018_22df6a62.png\" alt=\"negative 5\"></span> aren&rsquo;t solutions to the given equation.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":19,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959622,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"802549ac","skill_cd":"P.B.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","createDate":1691007959622,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"027749-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"51ac9902-64a1-498c-83b5-980692f40e0e","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"027749-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, x plus 2, close parenthesis, times, open parenthesis, x plus 3, close parenthesis, equals, open parenthesis, x minus 2, close parenthesis, times, open parenthesis, x minus 3, close parenthesis, plus 10\"></span></span></p></div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Which of the following is a solution to the given equation?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p>1</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p>0</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 2\"></span></p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 5\"></span></p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"a","rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. Applying the distributive property on the left- and right-hand sides of the given equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x squared, plus 2 x, plus 3 x, plus 6, equals, x squared, minus 2 x, minus 3 x, plus 6, plus 10\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x squared, plus 5 x, plus 6, equals, x squared, minus 5 x, plus 16\"></span>. Subtracting <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x squared \"></span> from and adding <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"5 x\"></span> to both sides of this equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"10 x plus 6, equals 16\"></span>. Subtracting 6 from both sides of this equation and then dividing both sides by 10 yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x equals 1\"></span>.<p>Choices B, C, and D are incorrect. Substituting 0, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 2\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 5\"></span> for <span class=\"italic\">x</span> in the given equation will result in a false statement. If <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x equals 0\"></span>, the given equation becomes <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"6 equals 16\"></span>; if <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x equals negative 2\"></span>, the given equation becomes <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 equals 30\"></span>; and if <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x equals negative 5\"></span>, the given equation becomes <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"6 equals 66\"></span>. Therefore, the values 0, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 2\"></span>, and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 5\"></span> aren&rsquo;t solutions to the given equation.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959622,"updateDate":1691007959622}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959622, 1691007959622),
    ($SATQ$821e724e$SATQ$, $SATQ$c52ea1c2-4bf1-4d4c-b86b-2dc95f66577b$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The function <math alttext="g"><mi>g</mi>
</math> is defined by <math alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals left parenthesis x plus 14 right parenthesis left parenthesis t minus x right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, where <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> is a constant. In the <em>xy</em>-plane, the graph of&nbsp;<math alttext="y equals g left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> passes through the point&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis 24 comma 0 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>24</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. What is the value of&nbsp;<math alttext="g left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced></math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["336"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["336"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math alttext="336"><mn>336</mn>
</math>. By the zero product property, if <math alttext="left parenthesis x plus 14 right parenthesis left parenthesis t minus x right parenthesis equals 0"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, then <math alttext="x plus 14 equals 0"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, which gives <math alttext="x equals negative 14"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis t minus x right parenthesis equals 0"><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, which gives <math alttext="x equals t"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mi>t</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, <math alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 0"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> when <math alttext="x equals negative 14"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn>
</mrow>
</math> and when <math alttext="x equals t"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mi>t</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Since the graph of <math alttext="y equals g left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> passes through the point&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis 24 comma 0 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, it follows that&nbsp;<math alttext="g left parenthesis 24 right parenthesis equals 0"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>24</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, so <math alttext="t equals 24"><mrow>
	<mi>t</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>24</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="24"><mn>24</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> in the equation <math alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals left parenthesis x plus 14 right parenthesis left parenthesis t minus x right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> yields <math alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals left parenthesis x plus 14 right parenthesis left parenthesis 24 minus x right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. The value of <math alttext="g left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced></math> can be calculated by substituting <math alttext="0"><mn>0</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> in this equation, which yields <math alttext="g left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis equals left parenthesis 0 plus 14 right parenthesis left parenthesis 24 minus 0 right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext="g left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis equals 336"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>336</mn></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"821e724e","external_id":"c52ea1c2-4bf1-4d4c-b86b-2dc95f66577b","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"3f16b7ed-bed9-48c8-98f6-cce56f9fdc28","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The function <math alttext=\"g\"><mi>g</mi>\n</math> is defined by <math alttext=\"g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals left parenthesis x plus 14 right parenthesis left parenthesis t minus x right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, where <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> is a constant. In the <em>xy</em>-plane, the graph of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"y equals g left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> passes through the point&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis 24 comma 0 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>24</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. What is the value of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"g left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced></mat